  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 808.27 Perfluorohexane Sulfonic Acid (PFHxS)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 808.27 Perfluorohexane Sulfonic Acid (PFHxS). For perfluorohexane sulfonic acid (PFHxS) violations, the statement shall read as follows:\n\n“Some people who drink water containing perfluorohexane sulfonic acid (PFHxS) in excess of the MCL over many years could experience problems with their liver, endocrine system, or immune system, or may experience increased cholesterol levels. It may also lower a woman’s chance of getting pregnant.”\n\nSource. #12838, eff 9-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw800.html"
